```

That sets the headings in capitals (text-transform uppercase), 16px, letter-spacing 0.08em. Note h2 base is 24px; we override. Also mobile media query sets h2 to 21px — specificity: `.page-products .section-title` (0,2,0) beats `h2` (0,0,1), so it holds at 16px on mobile too. That's fine.

Should the heading text itself be changed? "set the two section headings in capitals" — text-transform uppercase is standard for presentation. But tests may check computed style text-transform. Either works. Better to use CSS text-transform since it's a styling request and text content should stay readable for accessibility/screen readers. Actually screen readers can sometimes spell out all-caps text when the actual text is uppercase. Using text-transform is best practice.

